# state: any   (the golden cc9b4ced4a0f holds pathfind's profile; lane.accuracy804, #804)
# RalliSport Challenge (4D53000F): pathfind's recorded menu path (main menu RIGHT -> SINGLE RACE
# -> Rally -> Safari SS1 -> default car -> start race), then hands off the pad. Third capture:
# rallisport-804.route took CAREER (no rival ever in view); rallisport-804b.route held the hat
# for 0.35 s and the main menu auto-repeated from Career to OPTIONS
# (1791147878-lane.accuracy804-1639330 ended in Controller Settings).
#
# Fixed waits only (a dispatched soak gets the route's text; a `waitfor` crop does not travel).
# Route-relative times measured on 804b's log (the press sequence is identical, so they carry):
#   main menu shot +88.4; start-race A +140.3; spare A +148.6. Race clock 0 came 7.0 s after
#   the start-race A in capture 1 and in pathfind's replay, so race clock 0 ~+147.3 and the
#   rival stretch (race clock ~7.5 s on, flicker801) from ~+155. Shots r1-r7 run +152..+169.
#   A lost RIGHT sends the A presses down Career's path instead (shots `racetype`/`track` say so).
wait 20
shot boot20
wait 20
shot boot40
wait 20
mark booted
press START
wait 5
shot title
wait 3
press A
wait 6
press A
wait 6
shot mainmenu
# RIGHT exactly as pathfind sends it (pathfind.py send(): HATX max, HATX mid at once, then 0.35 s).
# 804b held the hat 0.35 s between max and mid: the menu auto-repeated past Single Race to Options.
axis HATX max
axis HATX mid
wait 2.35
press A
wait 6
shot racetype
press A
wait 6
shot track
press A
wait 6
shot car
press A
wait 25
shot options
press A
wait 8
press A
wait 3
shot r1
wait 2
shot r2
wait 2
shot r3
wait 2
shot r4
wait 2
shot r5
wait 3
shot r6
wait 3
shot r7
mark gameplay
repeat forever {
    wait 20
    shot hold
}
